    "What did you observe about the relationships between variables?\n",
    "\n",
    "Initial exploration suggests that employee satisfaction, average monthly hours, number of projects, years at the company, and salary level may be associated with employee turnover. Employees with lower satisfaction levels and heavier workloads appear more likely to leave the company. These relationships will be explored further through visualizations and statistical analysis.\n",
    "\n",
    "What do you observe about the distributions in the data?\n",
    "\n",
    "The dataset contains a mix of numerical and categorical variables. Some numerical variables appear to be skewed and contain outliers, particularly average monthly hours and tenure. Employee turnover is also imbalanced, with a larger proportion of employees remaining at the company than leaving.\n",
    "\n",
    "What transformations did you make with your data? Why did you choose to make those decisions?\n",
    "\n",
    "I standardized the column names using snake_case, corrected misspelled column names, removed duplicate records, and checked for missing values and outliers. These transformations improve data quality, consistency, and readability before building the predictive model.\n",
    "\n",
    "What are some purposes of EDA before constructing a predictive model?\n",
    "\n",
    "Exploratory data analysis helps identify patterns, detect missing values and outliers, understand relationships between variables, evaluate class balance, and determine which features are likely to contribute to the predictive model.\n",
